1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,698
Today, when we want an agent
to continue something we're doing online,

2
00:00:04,738 --> 00:00:07,565
we often have to explain the context again.

3
00:00:07,605 --> 00:00:12,263
We already clicked Singapore, Tokyo,
next week, two hundred dollars.

4
00:00:12,303 --> 00:00:15,528
Then we write a prompt
as if none of that happened.

5
00:00:16,128 --> 00:00:19,558
I'm choosing Singapore to Tokyo.
Next week.

6
00:00:19,598 --> 00:00:22,246
A hotel under two hundred dollars.

7
00:00:22,286 --> 00:00:23,914
Near a train station.

8
00:00:23,954 --> 00:00:25,304
A late departure.

9
00:00:25,344 --> 00:00:26,880
And a balanced trip.

10
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:29,106
I haven't written a prompt.

11
00:00:29,906 --> 00:00:34,368
The website converted those clicks
into structured intent.

12
00:00:34,408 --> 00:00:36,118
This sentence is for me.

13
00:00:36,158 --> 00:00:38,918
The agent will not parse the sentence.

14
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:42,506
It will call get current intent,
through WebMCP.

15
00:00:44,906 --> 00:00:48,700
Control just moved
from configuration to the agent.

16
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:50,684
The human had to press this.

17
00:00:50,724 --> 00:00:52,322
Nothing ran silently.

18
00:00:52,722 --> 00:00:55,795
The agent is not asking
where I'm going.

19
00:00:55,835 --> 00:01:00,264
It already has Singapore, Tokyo,
next week, two hundred,

20
00:01:00,304 --> 00:01:02,778
near transit, and a late flight.

21
00:01:03,278 --> 00:01:06,378
Best match cites the budget
and the station walk.

22
00:01:06,418 --> 00:01:11,823
The cheapest hotel was rejected
because it was twenty-four minutes from the station.

23
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:14,318
That preference survived the handoff.

24
00:01:15,018 --> 00:01:20,008
Now I change only the budget,
from two hundred to one hundred fifty.

25
00:01:20,048 --> 00:01:24,197
It kept Tokyo, next week,
late flight, near the station.

26
00:01:24,237 --> 00:01:25,890
Only the budget moved.

27
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:34,646
JoyRelay turns ordinary website interactions
into a language humans and agents can share.

